From d5eb8f34a81d536e71cacf84e45703c6ea133be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Albert Dahlin <info@albertdahlin.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 11:56:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Browser.Worker: natively compiled web workers

Runtime for the web workers feature in webbhuset/compiler: the
Worker.Program type that a worker module's main declares, spawn/send/
kill/stop, and the typed Channel/Worker handles. An effect manager
routes worker messages into the app via Platform.sendToApp; the kernel
harness (_Worker_run) is a minimal _Platform_initialize wired to the
worker's message port, so subscriptions and commands work normally
inside workers.

The compiler compiles each spawned worker program into its own bundle
next to the main one and replaces the program reference with that
file's name; both bundles share one compilation, so messages cross the
boundary as structured clones of ordinary Elm values, custom types
included, with no JSON encoding.

Versioned 1.0.3 as an unpublished fork version, consumed as a
git-dependency.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
